    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0360" n="310" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg310"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.85/8</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vladivostok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-17"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1918</hi></date>.
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 1.59 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Following telegram sent to-day at request Russian Volunteer Fleet, who state
                    their steamers detained Seattle: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Shestakovski, Russian Volunteer Fleet agent, New York: Steamships <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Nijni Novgorod, Kishinev, Toula</hi> are used
                            every year for regular Kamchatka trips, have no substitute as all our
                            steamers are working on regular lines during navigation as per
                            time-table; without said steamers needs of Kamchatka can not be
                            satisfied which will greatly affect not only Kamchatka’s population, who
                            have no communication during about five months, but also this country
                            and Russia where cargoes of fish caviar are imported. Without these
                            steamers, which are of larger size than others, Kamchatka will be <pb
                                facs="0361" n="311" xml:id="pg311"/> half satisfied which will ruin
                            fishing merchants working on Kamchatka every year. Kuzemenko.</p>
                        <p>I hereby confirm above statements. Caldwell, American Consul.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Steamers are required for Kamchatka fishing season and I request that they be
                    released.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Caldwell</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
